{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'CL_0001056|CL_0001057|CL_0001058|CD14|lacks expression|RO_0002292|lacks' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"1107:Declaration(Class(obo:CL_0001056))\n1108:Declaration(Class(obo:CL_0001057))\n1109:Declaration(Class(obo:CL_0001058))\n3537:Declaration(ObjectProperty(obo:RO_0002292))\n3711:# Object Property: obo:CL_4030045 (lacks_part)\n3714:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030045 \"lacks_part\")\n3716:# Object Property: obo:CL_4030046 (lacks_plasma_membrane_part)\n3719:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030046 \"lacks_plasma_membrane_part\")\n4098:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hematopoietic_stem_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000037 \"A stem cell from which all cells of the lymphoid and myeloid lineages develop, including blood cells and cells of the immune system. Hematopoietic stem cells lack cell markers of effector cells (lin-negative). Lin-negative is defined by lacking one or more of the following cell surface markers: CD2, CD3 epsilon, CD4, CD5 ,CD8 alpha chain, CD11b, CD14, CD19, CD20, CD56, ly6G, ter119.\")\n4163:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000041 \"Eosinophils are CD125-positive (IL-5R), GM-CSFR-positive, IL-3R-positive, VLA4-positive. They can also express MHC Class I & II, CD4, CD9, CD11a, CD11b, CD11c, CD13, CD15, CD16, CD17, CD18, CD24, CD25,CD28, CD29, CD32, CD33, CD35, CD37, CD39, CD43, CD44, CD45, CD45RB, CD45RO, CD46, CD47, CD48, CD49d, CD49f, CD50, CD52, CD53, CD54, CD55, CD58, CD59, CD62L, CD63, CD65, CD66, CD69, CD71, CD76, CD80, CD81, CD82, CD86, CD87, CD88, CD89, CD92, CD95, CD97, CD98, CD99, CD100, CD101, CD116, CD117, CD119, CD120, CD123, CD124, CD125, CD131, CD137, CD139, CD148, CD149, CD151, CD153, CD156, CD162, CD161, CD162, CD165, CD174, CD182, CD183, CD191, CD192, CD193, CD196, CD213, IL9R, ad integrin, beta-7 integrin, FceRI, IL13Ra1, TGFbR, PAFR, LTB4R, C3aR, CystLT1R, CystLT2R, fMLPR, CRTH2 (PGD2 receptor), histamine 4R, IDO, KYN, PAR-2, Siglec-8, Siglec-10, LIR1, LIR2, LIR3, LIR7, TLR7, TLR8, and VLA-4. Eosinophils can also secrete CXCL1, eotaxin-1, GM-CSF, IL-2, IL-3, IL-4, IL-5, IL-6, IL-8, IL-10, IL-12, IL-13, IL-16, IL-18, IFN-gamma, LTC4, MIP-1alpha, NGF, PAF, RANTES, substance P, TGF-alpha, TGF-beta, TNF-alpha, and VIP.\")\n4665:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000091 \"Markers: Mouse: F4/80+, CD11b-low, CD68+, sialoadhesin+, CD163/SRCR+; role or process: immune, antigen-presentation, clearance of senescent erythrocytes, iron metabolism. Kupffer cells are also reportedly C3aR-positive, CD14-low, CD54-positive, CD88-positive, and CD284-positive. They are also capable of producing IL-1, IL-6, TNF-alpha, nitric oxide, PGD2, PGE2, PGF2alpha, and TXA2.\")\n5062:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23616747\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000129 \"Unlike macroglial cells, microglial cells  arise from hematopoietic stem cells in the yolk sac during early embryogenesis that populate the central nervous system. They derive from embryonic mesoderm and are not from neuroectoderm where glioblast develops from. Markers: Mouse: CD11b+, F4/80+, CD68+. They represent ~12% of the cells in the CNS, but they are not uniformly distributed within the CNS. A normal adult mouse brain has approximately 3.5x10e6 microglia. Microglia are also reportedly CD3-negative, CD4-positive, CD8-negative, CD11b-positive, CD11c-high, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD45-low, CD56-negative, CD163-negative, CD200R-positive, CD281-positive, CD282-positive, CD283-positive, CD284-positive, CD285-positive, CD286-positive, CD287-positive, CD288-positive, CD289-positive, Gr1-negative, nestin-positive, and PU.1-positive.\")\n5117:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000134 \"Many but not all mesenchymal cells derive from the mesoderm. MSCs are reportedly CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD5-negative, CD8-negative, CD11a-negative, CD11b-negative, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD29-positive, CD31-negative, CD34-negative, CD38-negative, CD40-negative, CD44-positive, CD45-negative, CD49-positive, CD54-positive, CD66b-negative, CD79a-negative, CD80-negative, CD102-positive, CD106-positive, CD117-positive, CD121a-positive, CD121b-positive, CD123-positive, CD124-positive, CD133-negative, CD146-positive, CD166-positive, CD271-positive, B220-negative, Gr1-negative, MHCI-positive, MHCII-negative, SSEA4-negative, sca1-positive, Ter119-negative, and glycophorin A-negative. Cultured MSCs are capable of producing stem cell factor, IL7, IL8, IL11, TGF-beta, cofilin, galectin-1, laminin-receptor 1, cyclophilin A, and MMP-2.\")\n5128:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000135 \"Cultured human fibrocytes are MHCI-positive, MHCII-positive, CD1a-negative, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD8-negative, CD10-negative, CD11b-positive, CD13-positive, CD14-negative, CD16-negative, CD18-positive, CD19-negative, CD25-negative, CD29-positive, CD32-positive, CD33-negative, CD34-positive, CD38-negative, CD40-positive, CD44-negative, CD45RO-positive, CD49a-positive, CD49b-positive, CD49c-negative, CD49d-negative, CD49e-positive, CD49f-negative, CD56-negative, CD58-positive, CD61-positive, CD64-positive, CD70-negative, CD71-positive, CD80-positive, CD83-negative, CD86-positive, CD103-negative, CD105-positive, CD181-positive, CD182-negative, CD183-positive, CD184-positive, CD185-negative, CD186-negative, CD191-positive, CD192-negative, CD193-positive, CD194-positive, CD195-positive, CD196-negative, CD197-positive, CD199-positive, desmin-negative, F4/80-positive, Gr1-positive, LSP-1-positive, MHCI-positive, MHCII-positive, alpha-SMA-negative, TCRab-negative, TCRgd-negative, and vimentin-positive. Fibrocytes are also capable of secreting angiogenin, bFGF, CCL2, CCL3, CCL4, CCL8, CXCL1, type I collagen, type III collagen, CTGF, fibronectin, GM-CSF, IL-1a, IL-6, IL-8, IL-10, M-CSF, MMP-9, PDGF-A, TGF-alpha, TGF-beta1, TNF-alpha, and VEGF-A.\")\n5466:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000169 \"Pancreatic beta cells are also reportedly CD284-positive. Upon activation, they upregulate their CD14 expression.\")\n5949:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000225 \"A cell that lacks a nucleus.\")\n6018:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000233 \"Platelets are reportedly CCR1-positive, CCR2-negative, CCR3-positive, CCR4-positive, CCR5-negative, CCR6-negative, CCR7-negative, CCR8-negative, CCR9-negative, CCR10-negative, CD16-positive, CD23-positive, CD32-positive, CD40-positive, CD41-positive CD42-positive, CD61-positive, CD62P-positive, CD64-positive, CD89-positive, CD102-positive, CD147-positive (activated platelets), CD154-positive (activated platelets), CD162-positive, CD209, CD282-positive, CD284-positive, CD289-positive, CD181-negative, CD182-negative, CD183-negative, CD184-positive, CLEC2-positive, GPVI-positive, JAMC-positive, PAR1-positive, PAR2-negative, PAR3-positive, PAR4-positive, TSP1-positive, and TXA2R-positive. Platelets can reportedly produce CCL2, CCL3, CCL5, CCL7, CCL17, CD40L, CXCL1, CXCL4, CXCL4L1, CXCL5, CXCL7, CXCL8, CXCL12, EGF, factor V, factor VII, factor XI, factor XIII, bFGF, histamine, IGF-1, IL-1beta, PAI-1, PDGF, plasminogen, protein S, serotonin, TGF-beta, TFPI, VEGF, and vWF.\")\n7654:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000453 \"Originally described in the dendritic cell ontology (DC_CL:0000021 )(PMID:19243617). These cells are also CD1a-high, CD14-negative, CD207-positive (langerin), CD324-positive (E-cadherin), and DCIR-positive. They reside in the epidermis.\")\n8419:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1638021\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000547 \"An immature, nucleated erythrocyte occupying the stage of erythropoeisis that follows formation of erythroid progenitor cells. This cell is CD71-positive, has both a nucleus and a nucleolus, and lacks hematopoeitic lineage markers.\")\n8441:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000549 \"A nucleated immature erythrocyte, having cytoplasm generally similar to that of the earlier proerythroblast but sometimes even more basophilic, and usually regular in outline. The nucleus is still relatively large, but the chromatin strands are thicker and more deeply staining, giving a coarser appearance; the nucleoli have disappeared. This cell is CD71-positive and lacks hematopoeitic lineage markers.\")\n8454:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000550 \"A nucleated, immature erythrocyte in which the nucleus occupies a relatively smaller part of the cell than in its precursor, the basophilic erythroblast. The cytoplasm is beginning to acquire hemoglobin and thus is no longer a purely basophilic, but takes on acidophilic aspects, which becomes progressively more marked as the cell matures. The chromatin of the nucleus is arranged in coarse, deeply staining clumps. This cell is CD71-positive and lacks hematopoeitic lineage markers.\")\n8488:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000553 \"The earliest cytologically identifiable precursor in the thrombocytic series. This cell is capable of endomitosis and lacks expression of hematopoieitic lineage markers (lin-negative).\")\n8503:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000553 \"Lineage negative is described here as CD2-negative, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD5-negative, CD8a-negative, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD20-negative, CD56-negative, Ly6g-negative, and Ter119-negative.\")\n8623:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000564 \"A promyelocyte committed to the neutrophil lineage. This cell type is GATA-1-positive, C/EBPa-positive, AML-1-positive, MPO-positive, has low expression of PU.1 transcription factor and lacks lactotransferrin expression.\")\n8644:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000566 \"These cells are reportedly CD31-positive, CD34-positive, CD144-positive, CD309-positive, and TAL1-positive.\")\n8736:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000576 \"Morphology: Mononuclear cell, diameter, 14 to 20 _M, N/C ratio 2:1-1:1. Nucleus may appear in variety of shapes: round, kidney, lobulated, or convoluted. Fine azurophilic granules present; markers: CD11b (shared with other myeloid cells), human: CD14, mouse: F4/80-mid,GR1-low; location: Blood, but can be recruited into tissues; role or process: immune & tissue remodelling; lineage: hematopoietic, myeloid.\")\n9056:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000611 \"These cells are CD34-positive, CD45RA-negative, CD71-negative, and lineage-negative (CD2, CD3 epsilon, CD4, CD5, CD8a, CD14, CD19, CD20, integrin alpha-M, NCAM-1, SCA-1, Ly6G, Ly76).\")\n9074:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000613 \"A progenitor cell committed to the basophil lineage. This cell lacks hematopoietic lineage markers (lin-negative) and is CD34-positive, T1/ST2-low, CD117-negative, and FceRIa-high. This cell also expresses Gata-1, Gata-2 and C/EBPa.\")\n9079:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000613 \"BaP are also CD13-low and integrin beta-7-low. They are lin-negative (CD2, CD3e, CD4, CD5, CD8, CD11b, CD14, CD19, CD20, ly6g, ly76, and NCAM-1). They also lack expression of mast cell protease 1 (MCP-1) and microphthalmia-associated transcription factor (mitf).\")\n9195:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:mah\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41598-018-27692-8\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000626 \"A granule cell that has a soma located in an olfactory bulb granule cell layer. An olfactory granule cell is an interneuron that lacks an axon, makes reciprocal dendro-dendritic synapses with mitral cells and tufted cells and is involved in the fine spatio-temporal tuning of the responses of these principal olfactory bulb neurons to odors.\")\n9427:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0815332181\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21860392\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32097634\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WIKIPEDIA:Spinous_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000649 \"A keratinocyte found within the stratum spinosum (prickle cell layer) of the epidermis, distinguished by numerous intercellular desmosomes, which give it a “prickly” or spiny appearance. Positioned above the mitotically active basal layer and beneath the granular layer, it contributes to the skin’s mechanical strength and barrier function, preventing water loss and pathogen entry. This cell expresses differentiation-specific keratins K1 and K10 in mice, unlike basal cells that express K5 and K14, and lacks the keratohyalin granules found in granular cells, marking its intermediate stage of epidermal differentiation.\")\n9610:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000669 \"Pericytes are CD10-positive, CD13-positive, CD31-negative, CD45-negative, CD106-positive, CD117-negative, CD140-positive, CD144-negative, CD146-positive, CD271-positive, CD325-positive, NG2-positive, RGS5-positive, SMA-positive, and desmin-positive. A subpopulation is CD248-positive. They are also capable of producing angiopoietin 1, CXCL12, TGF-beta, and VEGF-A.\")\n10199:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000743 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005693))\n10299:EquivalentClasses(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27565351\") obo:CL_0000754 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000748 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P50481) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q8R4I7) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q9ER75)))\n10403:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18174176\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000765 \"A nucleated precursor of an erythrocyte that lacks hematopoietic lineage markers.\")\n10431:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000767 \"Matures in the bone marrow and account for <1% of leukocytes in the peripheral blood, spleen, and bone marrow. Basophils are described as being CD11a-positive, CD11b-positive, CD13-positive, CD15-positive, CD18-positive, CD21-positive, CD25-positive, CD29-positive, CD35-positive, CD40-positive, CD40L-positive, CD44-positive, CD45R-negative, CD46-positive, CD49a-positive, CD49b-positive, CD49d-positive, CD55-positive, CD59-positive, CD62L-positive, CD63-positive, CD69-positive, CD90-negative, CD116-positive, CD117-negative, CD124-positive, CD125-positive, CD131-positive, CD161-positive, CD184-positive, CD191-positive, CD192-positive, CD197-positive, CD200R3-positive, CD218-positive, CD282-positive, CD284-positive, CD289-positive, CD290-positive, CD294-positive, natural killer cell receptor 2B4-positive, smad1-positive, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD7-negative, CD8-negative, CD14-negative, CD15-negative, CD16-negative, CD19-negative, CD20-negative, CD34-negative, CD36-negative, CD45R-negative, CD56-negative, CD57-negative, CD235a-negative, and GR1-negative. Transcription factors- GATA1-positive, PU.1-positive.\")\n10477:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000771 \"Eosinophils are also CD14-negative, CD32-positive, CD44-positive, CD48-positive, CD69-positive, CD192-negative, MBP1-positive, MBP2-positive, TLR2-negative, TLR4-negative, and lineage-negative (B220, CD2, CD14, CD19, CD56, CD71, CD117, CD123, CD235a (glycophorin A), and TER119). The cytokines IL-3, IL-5, and GM-CSF are involved in their development and differentiation. Usually considered CD16-negative, CD16 is observed on eosinophilic metamyelocyte.\")\n10600:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000782 \"These cells are CD1a-negative, CD1b-positive, CD11a-positive, CD11c-positive, CD13-positive, CD14-negative, CD20-negative, CD21-negative, CD33-positive, CD40-negative, CD50-positive, CD54-positive, CD58-positive, CD68-negative, CD80-negative, CD83-negative, CD85j-positive, CD86-positive, CD89-negative, CD95-positive, CD120a-negative, CD120b-positive, CD123-negative, CD178-negative, CD206-negative, CD207-negative, CD209-negative, and TNF-alpha-negative. Upon TLR stimulation, they are capable of producing high levels of TNF-alpha, IL-6, CXCL8 (IL-8).\")\n11255:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000831 \"MCP are CD16-positive, CD32-positive, CD34-positive, CD45-positive, integrin beta-7-positive, and lin-negative (CD2, CD3e, CD4, CD5, CD8a, CD14, CD19, CD20, CD27, integrin alpha-M, ly6c, ly6g, NCAM-1, and ter119). These cells also express the transcription factors GATA-1, GATA-2, and MITF, but not C/EBPa.\")\n11725:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16507898\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37232741\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000881 \"A border associated macrophage that is adjacent to a small blood vessel of a brain. A perivascular macrophage expresses the markers CD14, CD16 and CD163. In homeostatic conditions, this central nervous system macrophage has a non-motile cell body with extending and retracting projections through the blood vessel wall.\")\n12414:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17100874\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000937 \"Cell committed to natural killer cell lineage that has the phenotype CD122-positive, CD34-positive, and CD117-positive. This cell type lacks expression of natural killer receptor proteins.\")\n12596:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18432934\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20839338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9785673\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000956 \"A pre-B-I cell is a precursor B cell that expresses CD34 and surrogate immunoglobulin light chain (VpreB , Lambda 5 (mouse)/14.1 (human)) on the cell surface, and TdT, Rag1,and Rag2 intracellularly. Cell type carries a D-JH DNA rearrangement, and lacks expression of immunglobulin heavy chain protein.\")\n13335:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17922016\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19286519\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001029 \"Common dendritic precursor is a hematopoietic progenitor cell that is CD117-low, CD135-positive, CD115-positive and lacks plasma membrane parts for hematopoietic lineage markers.\")\n13339:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001029 \"Surface markers are for mouse cells. Originally described in the dendritic cell ontology (DC_CL:0000041) CDP are reportedly CD2-negative, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD5-negative, CD8a-negative, CD11c-positive, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD20-negative, CD56-negative, B220-negative, Ly6g-negative, MHCII-positive, and Ter119-negative. (PMID:19243617).\")\n13567:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001053 \"A memory B cell that lacks expression of surface IgD.\")\n13574:# Class: obo:CL_0001054 (CD14-positive monocyte)\n13576:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001054 \"A monocyte that expresses CD14 and is negative for the lineage markers CD3, CD19, and CD20.\")\n13578:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001054 \"This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for 'monocyte'. Note that while CD14 is considered a reliable marker for human monocytes, it is only expressed on approximately 85% of mouse monocytes.\")\n13579:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001054 \"CD14-positive monocyte\")\n13583:# Class: obo:CL_0001055 (CD14-positive, CD16-low monocyte)\n13585:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20628149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001055 \"An intermediate monocyte that is CD14-positive and with low amounts of CD16.\")\n13588:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001055 \"CD14-positive, CD16-low monocyte\")\n13592:# Class: obo:CL_0001056 (dendritic cell, human)\n13594:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001056 \"A dendritic cell with the phenotype HLA-DRA-positive.\")\n13595:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0001056 \"dendritic cell\")\n13596:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001056 \"This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for 'dendritic cell'. The inclusion of HLA-DRA in the definition restricts this definition to human dendritic cells.\")\n13597:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001056 \"dendritic cell, human\")\n13598:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0001056 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000451 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002015) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)))\n13599:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0001056 obo:CL_0000451)\n13601:# Class: obo:CL_0001057 (myeloid dendritic cell, human)\n13603:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001057 \"A myeloid dendritic cell with the phenotype HLA-DRA-positive.\")\n13604:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0001057 \"myeloid dendritic cell\")\n13605:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001057 \"This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for 'myeloid dendritic cell'. The inclusion of HLA-DRA in the definition restricts this definition to human myeloid dendritic cells.\")\n13606:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001057 \"myeloid dendritic cell, human\")\n13607:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0001057 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000782 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002015) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)))\n13608:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0001057 obo:CL_0000782)\n13610:# Class: obo:CL_0001058 (plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human)\n13612:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001058 \"A plasmacytoid dendritic cell with the phenotype HLA-DRA-positive, CD123-positive, and CD11c-negative.\")\n13613:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0001058 \"plasmacytoid dendritic cell\")\n13614:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001058 \"This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for 'plasmacytoid dendritic cell'. The inclusion of HLA-DRA in the definition restricts this definition to human plasmacytoid dendritic cells.\")\n13615:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001058 \"plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human\")\n13616:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0001058 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000784 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_000001013) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001865) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002015) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)))\n13617:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0001058 obo:CL_0000784)\n13637:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001060 \"A hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell that has the ability to differentiate into limited cell types but lacks lineage cell markers and self renewal capabilities. Cell lacks hematopoeitic lineage markers.\")\n13697:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23292121\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23348417\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001065 \"A lymphocyte that lacks characteristic T cell, B cell, myeloid cell, and dendritic cell markers, that functions as part of the innate immune response to produce cytokines and other effector responses.\")\n13705:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001066 \"A progenitor cell committed to the erythroid lineage. This cell is ter119-positive but lacks expression of other hematopoietic lineage markers (lin-negative).\")\n14276:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002032 \"A hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell that has the ability to differentiate into limited cell types but lacks lineage cell markers and self renewal capabilities.\")\n14569:# Class: obo:CL_0002057 (CD14-positive, CD16-negative classical monocyte)\n14571:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15615263\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1706877\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19689341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002057 \"A classical monocyte that is CD14-positive, CD16-negative, CD64-positive, CD163-positive.\")\n14577:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002057 \"CD14-positive, CD16-negative classical monocyte\")\n14936:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002087 \"A leukocyte that lacks granules.\")\n15193:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002107 \"An IgD-negative CD38-positive IgG memory B cell is a CD38-positive IgG-positive that has class switched and lacks expression of IgD on the cell surface with the phenotype IgD-negative, CD38-positive, and IgG-positive.\")\n15288:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002117 \"A class switched memory B cell that lacks IgG on the cell surface.\")\n15303:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002118 \"A CD38-negative IgG-negative memory B cell is a IgG-negative class switched memory B cell that lacks IgG on the cell surface with the phenotype CD38-negative and IgG-negative.\")\n15310:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002119 \"A CD38-positive IgG-negative memory B cell is an IgG-negative class switched memory B cell that lacks IgG on the cell surface with the phenotype CD38-positive and IgG-negative.\")\n15317:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002120 \"An CD24-positive CD38-negative IgG-negative memory B cell is a CD38-negative IgG-negative class switched memory B cell that lacks IgG on the cell surface with the phenotype CD24-positive, CD38-negative, and IgG-negative.\")\n15324:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002121 \"A CD24-negative CD38-negative IgG-negative memory B cell is a CD38-negative IgG-negative class switched memory B cell that lacks IgG on the cell surface with the phenotype CD24-negative, CD38-negative, and IgG-negative.\")\n15331:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002122 \"A B220-positive CD38-positive IgG-negative memory B cell is a CD38-positive IgG-negative class switched memory B cell that lacks IgG on the cell surface with the phenotype B220-positive, CD38-positive, and IgG-negative.\")\n15338:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20123131\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002123 \"A B220-low CD38-positive IgG-negative memory B cell is a CD38-positive IgG-negative class switched memory B cell that lacks IgG on the cell surface with the phenotype B220-low, CD38-positive, and IgG-positive.\")\n15519:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002139 \"These cells are reportedly CD31-positive, CD34-positive, CD144-positive, TAL1-positive.\")\n15663:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002153 \"The dead keratin-filled squamous cell of the stratum corneum. This cell type lacks a nucleus.\")\n15737:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:5686391\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002161 \"A cell type found on the superficial layer of the external side of the tympanic membrane. This cell-type lacks a nucleus.\")\n16077:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0323052908\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myelocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002193 \"A cell type that is the first of the maturation stages of the granulocytic leukocytes normally found in the bone marrow. Granules are seen in the cytoplasm. The nuclear material of the myelocyte is denser than that of the myeloblast but lacks a definable membrane. The cell is flat and contains increasing numbers of granules as maturation progresses.\")\n16440:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002226 \"A secondary lens fiber cell that lacks a nucleus.\")\n16644:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002245 \"OBSOLETE: A lymphocyte that lacks T or B cell surface markers.\")\n17623:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002329 \"An epithelial cell type that lacks the columnar shape typical for other respiratory epithelial cells. This cell type is able to differentiate into other respiratory epithelial cells in response to injury.\")\n17703:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002338 \"Human markers; killer cell immunoglobulin-like receptor 2DL1 is used as a representative example (PRO at this time lacks a KIR superfamily).\")\n17729:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2673349\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002341 \"An undifferentiated cell of the prostate epithelium that lacks secretory activity.\")\n17737:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19652886\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002342 \"A circulating endothelial cell of the phenotype CD146-positive, CD105-positive, CD45-negative. This cell type is indicative of recent vascular damage.\")\n17761:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002344 \"Human markers; killer cell immunoglobulin-like receptor 2DL1 is used as a representative example (PRO at this time lacks a KIR superfamily).\")\n18079:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15580626\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30971890\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35815410\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002375 \"A multipotent progenitor cell that develops from a migratory neural crest cell. The schwann cell precursor is embedded among axons, with minimal extracellular space separating them from nerve cell membranes. This cell lacks a basal lamina, which distinguishes it from more mature Schwann cells. In rodents, cadherin-19 (Cdh19) serves as a specific marker for this developmental stage.\")\n18248:# Class: obo:CL_0002394 (CD141-positive myeloid dendritic cell)\n18250:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2882828\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2882837\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17332250\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20628149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002394 \"A myeloid dendritic cell found in the blood, lymph nodes, tonsil, bone marrow, and spleen that is CD141-positive (BDCA-3), XCR1-positive, and Clec9A-positive. This cell-type can cross-present antigen to CD8-positive T cells and can produce inteferon-beta.\")\n18254:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002394 \"CD141-positive myeloid dendritic cell\")\n18268:# Class: obo:CL_0002396 (CD14-low, CD16-positive monocyte)\n18270:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20870168\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002396 \"A patrolling monocyte that is CD14-low and CD16-positive.\")\n18275:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002396 \"CD14-low, CD16-positive monocyte\")\n18280:# Class: obo:CL_0002397 (CD14-positive, CD16-positive monocyte)\n18282:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20628149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21937707\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002397 \"A CD14-positive monocyte that is also CD16-positive and CCR2-negative.\")\n18286:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002397 \"This cell type is compatible with the HIPC Lyoplate markers for 'CD16+ monocyte'. Markers are associated with human cells. Note that this cell type encompasses both human intermediate monocytes (CD14+, CD16-low), and human non-classical monocytes (CD14-low, CD16+).\")\n18287:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002397 \"CD14-positive, CD16-positive monocyte\")\n19025:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002469 \"Gr1-high monocyte that lacks MHC-II receptor complex.\")\n19045:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002471 \"Gr1-low non-classical monocyte that lacks expression of a MHC-II complex.\")\n19216:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MP:0002407\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002489 \"A thymocyte that lacks expression of CD4 and CD8.\")\n19574:# Class: obo:CL_0002526 (CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell)\n19576:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19236899\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20309010\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002526 \"A dermal dendritic cell that is CD1a-negative and CD14-positive.\")\n19577:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002526 \"CD14+ dermal DC\")\n19579:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002526 \"CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell\")\n19583:# Class: obo:CL_0002527 (immature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell)\n19585:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002527 \"An immature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell is CD80-low, CD86-low, and MHCII-low.\")\n19586:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002527 \"immature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell\")\n19590:# Class: obo:CL_0002528 (mature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell)\n19592:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002528 \"A mature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell is CD80-high, CD86-high, MHCII-high and is CD83-positive.\")\n19593:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002528 \"mature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell\")\n19600:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20309010\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002529 \"A dermal dendritic cell that is CD1a-positive and CD14-negative.\")\n20542:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002629 \"Mature microglia are reportedly CCR2-positive, CD4-positive, CD9-positive, CD11a-positive, CD11b-positive, CD11c-positive, CD13-positive, CD16-positive, CDw17-positive, CD18-positive, CD21-positive, CD26-negative, CD32-positive, CD35-positive, CD36-positive, CD40-positive, CD44-positive, CD45-positive, CD53-positive, CD54-positive, CD56-negative, CD58-positive, CD63-positive, CD64-positive, CD66-positive, CD80-positive, CD86-positive, CD87-positive, CD92-positive, CD106-positive, CD107a-positive, CD147-positive, CD155-positive, CD162-positive, CD163-positive, CD171-negative, CD200R-positive, CXCR3-positive, CX3CR1-positive, fibronectin-positive, GD3-positive, GLUT1-positive, GLUT3-negative, GLUT5-positive, MHCI-positive, MHCII-positive, P2X4-positive, RFD7-negative, RGS5-negative, alpha-SMA-negative, vimentin-positive, and vwf-negative. Mature microglia are capable of producing BDNF, CCL3, CCL5, CCL7, CCL8, CCL9, CCL19, CCL20,CD40L, CSF, CXCL1, CXCL2, CXCL4, CXCL5, CXCL8, CXCL9, CXCL10, glutamate, IL-1beta, IL-1ra, IL-3, IL-6, IL-10, IL-12, LT, MMP-2, MMP-9, NGF, nitric oxide, ROS, TGF-beta, TNF-alpha.\")\n20670:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002643 \"An epithelial cell of stratum corneum of esophageal epithelium that lacks keratin.\")\n20917:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18353863\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19277783\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33193034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002668 \"A spiral ligament fibrocyte that is located in the triangular space inferior to the crista basilaris (basilar crest). This cell is spindle-shaped and expresses NKCC1 but minimal to no Na,K-ATPase (ATP1A1, ATP1B1) in mice and humans, and lacks connexin 26/30 in mice, indicating it does not participate in K⁺ recycling, unlike type II fibrocytes. Type IV fibrocyte is uniquely characterised by strong expression of connective tissue growth factor (CTGF) in mice, suggesting roles in tissue remodelling and paracrine signalling to other cochlear cells.\")\n21032:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20023630\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002679 \"A lymphocyte found in adipose tissue that lacks lineage markers of other lymphocytes but is capable of mediating TH2 cytokine responses. This cell type is found in fat associated lymphoid clusters, proliferates in response to IL2 and produce large amounts of TH2 cytokines such as IL5, IL6 and IL13\")\n21484:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0003035 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001243))\n23054:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0008032 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005110))\n23055:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0008032 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000007785))\n23056:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0008032 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000011467))\n25162:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0017009 obo:CL_0001056)\n25164:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0017009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_O43699))\n25165:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0017009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P30530))\n25461:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020003 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013502))\n25472:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020004 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015665))\n25529:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000011241))\n25534:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22726837\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25843402\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25926446\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27194328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37336974\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020010 \"A GABAergic projection neuron located in the external segment of the globus pallidus (GPe) and defined by its exclusive projection to the dorsal striatum rather than to the subthalamic nucleus or basal ganglia output nuclei. In rodents and primates, it is characterized molecularly by expression of FOXP2, MEIS2, and NPAS1, and lacks expression of canonical pallidal markers NKX2-1 and LHX6 (Dodson et al., 2015; Abdi et al., 2015; Courtney et al., 2023). This neuron is GABAergic (GAD1/2⁺, SLC32A1/VGAT⁺) and typically PV⁻, forming the transcriptionally and developmentally LGE-derived subclass of GPe neurons (Dodson et al., 2015; Mallet et al., 2012).\")\n25568:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003675))\n25569:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005694))\n25570:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P16444))\n25584:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020014 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001243))\n25600:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34280086\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.12.07.570646\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020016 \"A tissue-specific stem cell with long-term self-renewal capacity that is restricted to generating bone, cartilage, and stromal cell lineages. This cell is primarily located in the growth plate (resting zone), periosteum, and subchondral bone regions, and is marked by high clonogenicity and robust multipotent differentiation potential in both osteogenic and chondrogenic lineages. Distinctively, ocSSC lacks adipogenic capacity, distinguishing it from other mesenchymal stem cell populations.\")\n25633:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\n25634:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000007498))\n25658:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36338137\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020021 \"A mesenchymal progenitor cell located in fibrocartilaginous tissues, along the fibrochondrocytic differentiation pathway that co-expresses both fibrochondrocyte markers (COL1A1, COL3A1) and mesenchymal stem cell markers (MCAM/CD146, MYLK) in humans. This cell serves as a progenitor for mature fibrochondrocytes and other meniscal cell types, with differentiation regulated by TGF-β signaling, focal adhesion, and extracellular matrix-receptor interaction pathways.\")\n25733:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020027 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to increases in light intensity. It possesses the large soma and expansive dendritic field characteristic of alpha RGCs (Krieger et al., 2017). This cell exhibits a brief, fast-decaying burst of firing at the onset of light increments and contributes to motion detection for luminance increases, forming the ON-branch of the transient magnocellular-like pathway (Krieger et al., 2017; Hahn et al., 2023). Functionally, it corresponds to cluster G19 and aligns transcriptomically with cluster C41 (Krieger et al., 2017; Tran et al., 2019). It is orthologous to the primate ON Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). Molecularly, it expresses Spp1, Smi32, and Brn3b, but lacks Brn3a, Brn3c, and Calbindin (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\n26204:SubClassOf(obo:CL_1000308 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013031))\n30019:SubClassOf(obo:CL_2000096 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q15063))\n30169:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P32648))\n30206:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023010 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005460))\n30216:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023011 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000032148)))\n30253:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023014 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P32648))\n30263:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023015 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015325)))\n30265:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023015 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015325))\n30283:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023016 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000017299)))\n30287:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023016 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000017299))\n30300:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023017 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023069 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015665)))\n30317:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013502))\n30326:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023019 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023071 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P32648)))\n30355:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023022 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q9D387))\n30370:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023023 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q9D387))\n30385:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023024 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q9D387))\n30398:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023025 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\n30410:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023026 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001175))\n30426:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023027 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\n30440:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023028 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\n30452:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023029 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001177))\n30468:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023030 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\n30483:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023031 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\n30538:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013502))\n30754:SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30096314\") obo:CL_4023056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P11087))\n30755:SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30096314\") obo:CL_4023056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P26618))\n30756:SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30096314\") obo:CL_4023056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P51885))\n30842:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023065 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000010317))\n30908:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023071 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P09240))\n30946:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023075 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P24529))\n30947:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023075 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\n31068:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30715238\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023093 \"A pyramidal neuron which lacks a tuft formation but extends small radial distances forming a star-like shape.\")\n31084:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30715238\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023095 \"A pyramidal neuron which lacks a clear tuft formation but extends to large radial distances.\")\n31293:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023118 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\n31304:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023119 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015426))\n31327:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023121 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005444))\n31328:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023121 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015665))\n31341:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023122 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001635))\n31342:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023122 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015665))\n31368:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023125 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023123 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000012526) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000016004)))\n31405:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023130 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000009344)))\n31522:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023181 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015658))\n31911:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4030026 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000584 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q8NFU0)))\n32028:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030038 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001786))\n32029:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030038 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001932))\n32030:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030038 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000017298))\n32135:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030050 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001175))\n32136:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030050 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001177))\n32149:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030051 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001175))\n32163:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030052 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001177))\n32176:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030053 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001175))\n32189:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030054 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001175))\n32190:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030054 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001666))\n32344:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4030068 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023040 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0005395) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000004919)))\n32357:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4032000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000014505))\n32367:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4032001 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013879)))\n32767:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033041 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000002123))\n32838:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25564622\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34044844\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35387001\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37834236\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033048 \"A respiratory epithelial cell derived from a basal cell, with a topographic nuclear position between the basal and luminal cells of the airway epithelium. This non-basal, intermediate progenitor cell has limited proliferative capacity and can differentiate into multiciliated, secretory, or rare airway cells (ionocytes, tuft cells, neuroendocrine cells). It shares some ultrastructural features with basal cells but lacks the defined characteristics of fully differentiated cellular phenotypes.\")\n32935:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19648928\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35617956\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033057 \"A luminal epithelial cell of the mammary gland that can proliferate and has the potential to differentiate into a lactocyte during pregnancy. In humans, a luminal adaptive secretory precursor cell can be identified by high levels of the markers EpCAM and CD49f, and in mice it can be identified by low levels of CD29 and high levels of CD14, Kit, CD61, and Tspan8.\")\n33045:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21918187\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30755708\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33150420\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033065 \"A mature B cell that serves as an intermediate stage in the differentiation of naive B cells into a plasmablast. A preplasmablast expresses CD30 and IL-6R and lacks expression of CD20, CD23, CD38 and CD138.\")\n33135:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033086 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000016626))\n33196:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033092 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000584 ObjectSomeValues